            <ArticleTitle>Backfire: AHCPR practice guideline for acute low back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>465-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The AHCPR &quot;Guideline for Acute Low Back Problems in Adults&quot; is a must-read for every South Carolina physician treating low back pain. The 25-page pamphlet excels as a practical guide for swiftly triaging acute low back problems into the 90 percent majority who recover within a month, from the few &quot;red flag&quot; and &quot;red herring&quot; serious back problems requiring urgent attention. But the Guideline panel overstepped its policymaking mandate by venturing into the quicksand of treatment by committee edict, rather than by on-the-spot caretakers. The rumbling backfire is that U. S. Government document, intended as practice guideline for routine acute back care, will come to haunt us as a practice standard for all back care. One-size-fits-all proposals for the majority short-change the few with more demanding healthcare resource requirements. Be sure to read the pamphlet; your patients, insurers, providers, administrators, journalists and attorneys will!</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
